<title>GREECE: CITIBANK, ATHENS TO CUT BASE DEPO RATES BY 50 BPS.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK, ATHENS TO CUT BASE DEPO RATES BY 50 BPS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will cut its base savings</p>
<p>rate structure by 50 basis points, and re-price its save plus,</p>
<p>save plus 12, check plus and gold plus accounts effective</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>It also kept its special current account for individuals and</p>
<p>its interest bearing current account for companies unchanged.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following lending rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 16.25 percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 17.00 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 16.50 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 16 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 23 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 21 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans at 18.75 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Base rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for</p>
<p>the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  8.00 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.88 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  2.97 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.59 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.67 percent</p>
<p>    Pounds Sterling:  8.81 percent</p>
<p>    French francs  :  5.84 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  4.31 percent</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
